  "sources": [
    {
      "file": "ddraw-colorkey-surface.c",
      "blobSha1": "b9300a98cf801690399d5f08f6977685123357b5",
      "sha256": "d24845b55037dac48f5dd5ce84cbed4d35cd0fc06e3ba419413dabdd484e8dd9",
      "url": "https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/415a275e3844c252ad385b46023095e9401ca234/dlls/ddraw/surface.c",
      "evidence": "surface1_Flip: validate named member/self, rotate unnamed storage, exchange front/named storage without rotating intermediate members, update primary frontbuffer only for a primary. Implementation evidence; no fresh original HAL execution."
    }
  ],
  "scope": "S2-51: nonprimary Flip never copies its source 1:1 into the primary retained base. Default ring rotation and named front/target exchange move handle/storage/memory/shadow/external/upload-debt together while preserving public identity, keys, palette and overlay id. Rebind affected visible overlay source/destination handles after rotation; present only a primary or a change affecting a visible overlay. Hidden/unrelated offscreen flips do not present. Self/unrelated/foreign named targets are refused before mutation; accepted storage prefixes are retained on transport presentation failure. Actual native C: 2830 checks, 512 two/three-buffer default/named flips, coupled fields, destination rebinding, stable overlay identity, primary base and invalid-target isolation; thirteen runtime mutations, sanitizer and old actual Flip with current helper definitions runtime control. XP five surface Flip interfaces on one three-buffer overlay: fifteen visible and five hidden successful flips, ten refused self/unrelated calls, one silent offscreen flip and 46 CPU shadow checks. Thirty-seven observed frames use twenty-two explicit primary background controls after queued SHOW/HIDE (these API calls are not asserted to present immediately); actual Flip frames contain no base write. Thirty-six overlay records, twenty-two uploads, 276 key restatements. Independent GPU replay verifies all 28416 retained-base pixels and all 28416 displayed-composite pixels per backend, distinguishing a stable primary base from the 16x12 overlay at (8,6). No CPU pixel reply is used. Existing 32x24 virtual mode fallback, not native mode/HAL acceptance. Seven textures, four explicit physical destructions; three known implicit guest child/storage leaks remain S2-53 and are preserved in the graph. Broad flip caps/lock/DC/format/interval policy, external descriptor-pointer semantics, arbitrary callback/thread/device-loss/ownership conversion, S2-52/53/54/55/57, games/FPS and review stages 4/5/6 remain open. D3D8/9 and host/protocol/shader/bundle unchanged.",
